# Canonical identities, so `git log`, `git shortlog` and `git blame` show one
# name per person. Half the history was committed under a GitHub noreply
# identity whose display name is a typo of the author's own name; rewriting 147
# commits to fix it would change every hash and throw away the development
# history this repository is meant to show, which is what .mailmap exists to
# avoid. Nothing about the commits themselves changes.
#
#   <canonical name> <canonical email> <name as committed> <email as committed>
